On 01/03/2015 22:51, David Carlisle wrote:
> I'm wondering if after all we should "suggest" an update to etex.sty
> that doesn't over-write the allocation system on new formats. If (as
> in this case) etex.sty is loaded late after the new allocation scheme
> has already allocated into the extended range, the etex scheme won't
> look in count11-19 to see where to pick up the extended range it will
> always start allocating from 271 so you will get double allocations.
> It would be possible to fix that echoing the allocation numbers into
> the etex counts
> but that adds a lot of complication for what should be a temporary problem.
> 
> I think having etex.sty detect 2015 and not trample on the new
> allocation scheme (but define
> stubs for \resereinserts and \globcount etc may work better, despite
> having argues against that earlier.

Updating etex.sty is fine but I don't think that the cost can be
disabling \loccount, etc. That's a fundamental part of etex.sty and more
importantly having it perhaps work one way and perhaps another
(depending on kernel version) seems like a very bad idea.

